<https://w3id.org/chronicle-usage-ontology/core.owl.ttl>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "chronicle-usage-ontology-core" ;
    dcterms:license "MIT" ;
    dcterms:title "Chronicle Android Usage Measurement — Research Ontology (core module)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1177/21522715261417288> ;
    skos:definition """Core entity model for the Android UsageStatsManager event-log -> usage-measurement research ontology. Implements the D4 five-way split from docs/workflow/research-ontology-design.md (occurrence / record / optional logging-observation / assertion / execution / interval) so provenance can always distinguish what was OBSERVED from what was RECONSTRUCTED, and so absence and unresolved attribution can never silently drop from denominators.
Backbone (D2, upper-neutral): SOSA/SSN + OWL-Time + PROV-O + P-Plan. BFO-vs-DOLCE is deliberately deferred and, when needed, bridged via SSSOM — this module asserts only the free, standards-grounded mappings. This is the FOUNDATION module: SHACL axioms, BCIO/Shaleha close-mappings, DQV quality, and generator wiring are later build-order steps (doc 13 §"Prioritized build order").""" ;
    skos:note "Screen-use measurement framework alignment (Shaleha, Roque, Andrews, Calfee & Lee 2026, doi:10.1177/21522715261417288): this ontology's measures sit on the framework's OBJECTIVE-LOG / passive-sensing modality axis. Referenced, not class-mapped, because the framework has no stable class IRIs." ;
.

chron:AppFeatureSessionRecord
