    skos:broadMatch prov:Entity ;
    skos:definition "Supplied tracked-app session containing separately identified interruption intervals, not continuous app use or unlock-to-lock device use. Why Did you Stop (2021), author-copy physical p.3 Section3.2 and p.7 Section4.4.2, records each interruption individually within a learning session. Figure1 p.4 illustrates independent session/interruption times and app labels. Meaningful (3191754) primary279-284 uses one before/during/after sampling timing per app instance, not three waves within every instance. Supplied session answers, optional interruption references and independent quantities retain their own definitions. Package identity is independent of an optional printed app label. IDs and pairing are normalized, not recovered raw serialization. Unknown membership is not observed zero. No timer, constructor, return-to-learning, interruption cause, scoring, last-interruption selection, ESQ eligibility or duration is inferred." ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/chronicle-usage-ontology/core> ;
.

chron:ComplianceDayAssessment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ComplianceDayAssessment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_percent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:meets_compliance_threshold ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:expected_device_count ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:known_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_percent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:unknown_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:meets_compliance_threshold ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:expected_device_count ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:float ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_percent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:string ;
            owl:onProperty chron:participant_id ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:zero_eligible_usage ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:participant_id ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:boolean ;
            owl:onProperty chron:meets_compliance_threshold ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:known_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:float ;
            owl:onProperty chron:known_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:unknown_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:float ;
            owl:onProperty chron:unknown_minutes ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:integer ;
            owl:onProperty chron:expected_device_count ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:date ;
            owl:onProperty chron:date ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:sharing_status ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:participant_id ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:zero_eligible_usage ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_value_basis ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:boolean ;
            owl:onProperty chron:zero_eligible_usage ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:date ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:sharing_status ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom chron:ComplianceValueBasis ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_value_basis ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_value_basis ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:date ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_threshold_percent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom chron:DeviceSharingStatus ;
            owl:onProperty chron:sharing_status ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_threshold_percent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:float ;
            owl:onProperty chron:compliance_threshold_percent ;
        ] ;
    skos:broadMatch prov:Entity ;
    skos:definition """One participant-day row of the `compliance_csv` — the compliance measure this engine actually computes. Its slots mirror the CSV columns: the eight-field `ComplianceDayCheckpoint` (pipeline_v2.rs) plus `expected_device_count`, which the writer joins from the enrolled-devices support file at write time; `compliance_threshold_percent` is the scalar input the engine compares against (not a CSV column), and `compliance_value_basis` is this ontology's own name for the imputation distinction, present in no engine output. This term exists because AttributionStatus formerly claimed to BE the compliance denominator contract while nothing described the quantity, its denominator, or its defaults.
WHAT THE DENOMINATOR ADMITS. `accumulate_minutes` (pipeline_v2_incremental.rs) walks the output rows and adds `duration_minutes` to the day's bucket only when the row's interaction type is App Usage or Non-Target Participant App Usage AND `minimum_duration_aggregate_eligible` is set. Numerator = minutes whose username is neither blank, "nan", nor "None"; denominator = numerator plus the rest.
WHAT IT SILENTLY EXCLUDES, in every case without a receipt in this output: (1) Filtered App Usage — excluded packages are RELABELLED rather than deleted, keep their raw evidence, and are then absent from both numerator and denominator, so package-exclusion policy moves this measure; (2) episodes ruled ineligible by the minimum-duration disposition, so a sub-floor episode's minutes are attributed to nobody; (3) any episode whose duration is blank, which contributes 0.0; (4) every non-app row type, including End of Usage Missing — so an episode zeroed by the long-duration cap leaves the denominator entirely. The compliance percent is therefore a share of ADMITTED minutes, never a share of the participant's day.
THE 100.0 DEFAULT IS AN IMPUTATION. When the participant is not in the device-sharing file, or when the admitted total for the day is zero, the engine writes compliance_percent = 100.0 without measuring anything, and `is_valid` then compares that literal against the threshold like any other value — so an unshared participant and a participant with no qualifying usage both count as valid days. The distinction survives only in `sharing_status` and `zero_real_usage`; compliance_value_basis is this ontology's name for it, so a summary of the percent column can state which rows it measured and which it inherited.
The participant-day spine is every (participant, date) pair seen on any APP-output row — the screen output is not consulted — including rows contributing no minutes, so a day can appear here with a zero total and a 100.0 percent.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/chronicle-usage-ontology/core> ;
.

chron:CoverageAssessment
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CoverageAssessment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:minCardinality 0 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:expected_available ;
        ] ,
        [
