            owl:onProperty chron:device_id ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom xsd:float ;
            owl:onProperty chron:availability_threshold ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:maxCardinality 1 ;
            owl:onProperty chron:coverage_cause ;
        ] ;
    skos:definition """A coverage/observability judgement over a stream window: expected vs actual data availability, its threshold, bounding events, and best-supported cause. A gap MAY CONCEAL usage — this asserts only how the measurement policy treats the interval, never that the device was inactive.
DESIGN-TIME ONLY, like the CoverageCause it carries: no kernel path emits an expectation, an availability threshold, a policy treatment, or a cause. The coverage judgement this engine ships is the per-day DayCoverageAssessment. Keep the two apart when reading an instance graph — this class describes a window-level cause attribution that is available to an author, not a reading of pipeline output.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/chronicle-usage-ontology/core> ;
.

